message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on a Wi-Fi controlled extension cord. Candidates are 8544.42.9090 (insulated electric conductors fitted with connectors, for voltage not exceeding 1,000 V) and 8536.50 (switches). The cord with a switch module would still be classified as an insulated conductor fitted with connectors, under 8544.42. Alternatively, the item could be a power strip-like device under 8536.69 (plugs and sockets). I recall that the ruling for a "Wi-Fi controlled extension cord" classified it in 8544.42.9090, so I am going with that.

Within 8544.42, the 8544.42.20 subheading covers telecommunication cables, 8544.42.90 covers other, and 8544.42.9090 is the statistical suffix for other.

{"hts_code": "8544.42.9090", "reason": "A 16 AWG insulated copper cord fitted with a plug and receptacles for voltage not over 1,000 V is an insulated electric conductor fitted with connectors under heading 8544, and the inline Wi-Fi switch module does not change that classification."}
